# Astro Dashboard Architecture Rules

## Layout Shell Strategy
- Enforce a fixed **App Shell** layout: persistent Sidebar, Top Header, and dynamic `<main>` viewport.
- Render all structural components (Sidebar navigation, Header profile, Metric Cards) strictly server-side using pure Astro components (`.astro`).
- Do NOT wrap entire dashboard pages in client framework boundaries (React/Svelte/Vue). Keep page structures static and hydrate only dynamic widgets.

## Server-Side Data Loading
- Load primary metrics, user permissions, and initial dataset summaries directly inside the Astro frontmatter (`---` block) via Server-Side Rendering (SSR) or Astro Actions.
- Wrap data fetching in typed DTO getters (e.g., `getDashboardStats(Astro.locals)`).

```astro
---
// GOOD: Server-side data fetching in Astro frontmatter
import { getAnalyticsSummary } from '@/lib/api/analytics';
import MetricCard from '@/components/dashboard/MetricCard.astro';

const user = Astro.locals.user;
if (!user) return Astro.redirect('/login');

const stats = await getAnalyticsSummary(user.tenantId);
---

<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
  <MetricCard title="Revenue" trend="{stats.revenueTrend}" value="{stats.formattedRevenue}"/>
</div>